# 9. PROJECT MANAGEMENT WORKFLOW

Create a backend-controlled project lifecycle.

Every project must have a unique project ID.

Each project must be associated with:

- Customer ID.
- Project ID.
- Service category.
- Project details.
- Project files.
- Price estimate, if available.
- Project status.
- Status history.
- Admin.
- Customer communications.
- Created date.
- Updated date.
- Completion date, if applicable.

### Project status workflow

Request Submitted → Reviewing → Accepted → Editing in Progress → Ready for Review → Completed.

Additional states:

- Rejected.
- Cancelled.
- Waiting for Customer Information.
- Revision Requested.

### Revision workflow

Ready for Review → Revision Requested → Editing in Progress → Ready for Review.

### Status rules

- Customers submit project requests.
- Admin reviews requests.
- Admin accepts or rejects requests.
- Admin controls project status.
- Customers view their own status.
- Customers request revisions when permitted.
- Admin communicates through project updates.
- Admin marks projects completed.
- Status changes must be recorded.
- Invalid status transitions must be rejected.
- Cancelled projects must follow defined rules.

Implement project state transitions on the backend.

Never allow customers to directly modify project status fields.

